! FatesNvp: run FATES with the moss (non-vascular phototroph) PFT enabled.
!
! The switch and the parameter file travel together: with use_fates_moss true, FATES
! requires a parameter file whose fates_litterclass dimension is 8, and with it false it
! requires 6. Setting either alone aborts at initialization, by design.
!
! use_bedrock is deliberately absent: it lives in the FatesALP2* testmods.
!
! This is the general-purpose moss testmod. FatesMossParams is identical to it today but
! stays minimal, because its only job is to exercise the 8-litterclass parameter file
! against a non-moss fsurdat. Do not consolidate the two: new moss history variables are
! added HERE as they are implemented, which is what will make them diverge.
!
! Those additions MUST use the append form:
!     hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_SOME_MOSS_VARIABLE'
! A plain `hist_fincl1 = ...` would REPLACE, not extend. CIME applies testmods in order and
! later ones win (cime/CIME/user_mod_support.py), and the nocomp test composes this testmod
! after clm/Fates, which sets hist_empty_htapes plus the 71-variable FATES list. Assigning
! here would silently wipe FATES_FUEL_AMOUNT, FATES_BURNFRAC and the rest -- on the only two
! tests that run SPITFIRE. It would look harmless on the SP tests, which do not include
! clm/Fates.

use_fates_moss = .true.
fates_paramfile = '$SRCROOT/src/fates/parameter_files/fates_params_moss.json'

hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_LIVEMOSS_FUEL'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_MOSS_FINES'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_MOSS_FWET_LIQ'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_MOSS_FWET_TOT'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_MOSS_FWET_SOIL_LIQ'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_MOSS_FWET_SOIL_TOT'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_MOSS_FWET_CANOPY'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_MOSS_WETNESS_SCALER'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_MOSS_HEIGHT'

! Instantaneous total (liquid plus ice) soil water, the CTSM field FATES_MOSS_FWET_SOIL_TOT is
! checked against. The empty-tapes setting from clm/Fates removes it otherwise, and a daily
! mean would not match the FATES field's once-daily value.
hist_fincl1 += 'H2OSOI:I'

! Existing FATES per-PFT and per-fuel-class diagnostics that the moss science
! checks need read out for the moss PFT and for fuel classes 7 (live moss) and 8 (dead
! moss). They are not moss-specific variables, which is why they are not covered by the
! block above.
!
! They are requested here because the two SPITFIRE-enabled tests -- the I2000Clm60Fates
! nocomp entries, the only ones where fire runs at all -- set hist_empty_htapes via
! clm/Fates, and clm/Fates's hist_fincl1 lists none of these. Without these lines those
! two tests emit nothing usable for moss fuel loading, moss fuel moisture, moss GPP or
! moss mortality.
!
! FATES_LEAFC_PF and FATES_CROWNAREA_PF are here for the moss leaf-biomass allometry:
! leaf carbon per m2 land area, and the crown area that converts it to per m2 crown
! area.
!
! On the FATES-SP tests these come back as zeros -- the fire ones because SP mode cannot
! run SPITFIRE (build-namelist makes fates_spitfire_mode > 0 fatal under use_fates_sp),
! the mortality ones because SP bypasses the demographic paths. hist_fincl1 wins over
! hist_fexcl1, so the fire entries appear on the SP tapes despite fates_sp excluding
! them. Zeros there are the correct reading, not a defect.
!
! FATES_NOCOMP_PATCHAREA_PF is registered only when nocomp is on (nocomp_if in
! FatesHistoryInterfaceMod). Every test composing this testmod today has nocomp on -- SP
! forces it, and the fire tests compose FatesColdNoCompFixedBioGeo. If this testmod is
! ever composed with full competition, drop that line: naming an unregistered field in
! hist_fincl1 is a hard endrun, not a warning.

hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_FUEL_MOISTURE_FC'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_FUEL_AMOUNT_FC'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_FUEL_BURNT_BURNFRAC_FC'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_GPP_PF'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_LEAFC_PF'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_CROWNAREA_PF'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_NOCOMP_PATCHAREA_PF'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_MORTALITY_HYDRAULIC_PF'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_MORTALITY_TERMINATION_PF'

! Moss leaf and stem area index. Each is the per-PFT sum of ccohort%treelai (resp.
! ccohort%treesai) times ccohort%c_area*AREA_INV over every cohort of the PFT, in
! every canopy layer and size class.
!
! Note the normalization: these are per m2 LAND area. Dividing FATES_LAI_PF by
! FATES_CROWNAREA_PF recovers ccohort%treelai itself, per m2 CROWN area, which is the
! quantity the moss leaf-biomass allometry is reasoned about in.

hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_LAI_PF'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_SAI_PF'

! RAIN is a CLM field rather than a FATES one, and the only non-FATES variable this
! testmod asks for. It is here because the moss wetness proxy's canopy ingredient is
! CTSM's fwet_veg, which exists only because rain was intercepted by the canopy: whether
! that ingredient is event-driven, and whether its events are rain events, cannot be
! asked at all unless the forcing that drives it is on the same tape.
!
! 'RAIN' and not 'RAIN_FROM_ATM': RAIN is forc_rain_downscaled_col, the rain remaining
! after rain/snow repartitioning by temperature (biogeophys/Wateratm2lndType.F90:184),
! which is what actually reaches the canopy. RAIN_FROM_ATM is the pre-repartitioning
! flux, and at an arctic site the difference between the two is most of the year.
!
! RAIN is registered active by default, so this line changes nothing on the FATES-SP
! tests, which do not compose clm/Fates and so carry the full default CLM field list
! already. It is the I2000Clm60Fates nocomp entries that need it: clm/Fates sets
! hist_empty_htapes there, which drops every default CLM field including this one.

hist_fincl1 += 'RAIN'

! Instrumentation for the moss-extinction diagnosis: in the ALP2 nocomp run the moss
! cohort is culled while still holding a large fraction of its peak leaf carbon, and
! nothing recruits behind it. These read out, per PFT, the moss carbon pools, the
! productivity feeding them, every mortality term that could remove the cohort, and the
! whole seed/seedling/recruitment chain that would replace it. FATES_ELONG_FACTOR_PF is
! here in case partial abscission, rather than mortality, is what empties the leaves.
!
! Every name below is registered unconditionally inside the hlm_hist_level_dynam > 1
! block of FatesHistoryInterfaceMod (if_dyn1), which the default
! fates_history_dimlevel = 2,2 satisfies and which no testmod composed with this one
! overrides. Several are registered use_default='inactive'; that does not matter here,
! because hist_fincl1 activates them.
!
! FATES_MORTALITY_CSTARV_PF is the per-PFT sum of FATES_MORTALITY_CSTARV_SZPF, so it
! includes termination-by-C-starvation. FATES_MORTALITY_TERMINATION_PF, requested above,
! deliberately excludes that same term, so the two do not double-count.

hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_NPLANT_PF'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_STOREC_PF'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_VEGC_PF'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_NPP_PF'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_MORTALITY_CSTARV_CFLUX_PF'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_MORT_CSTARV_CONT_CFLUX_PF'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_MORTALITY_CSTARV_PF'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_MORTALITY_PF'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_MORTALITY_CFLUX_PF'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_SEED_BANK_PF'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_SEEDS_IN_PF'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_SEEDLING_POOL_PF'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_UNGERM_SEED_BANK_PF'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_RECRUITMENT_PF'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_RECRUITMENT_CFLUX_PF'
hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_ELONG_FACTOR_PF'

! Moss's transpiration wetness factor, per PFT. The moss rooting profile is now the
! top-layer profile mode (FATES fnrt_prof_mode = 5): the whole profile in soil layer 1,
! exactly nothing below it. So moss's btran is a function of the top layer alone, and the
! measurement this instruments is "was moss's btran zero on this day, and how wet was the
! top layer when it was" -- FATES_MOSS_FWET_SOIL_LIQ, requested above, is the companion.
!
! FATES_BTRAN_PF and not FATES_BTRAN_SZPF: the latter is filled from ccohort_hydr%btran
! and so is identically zero without FATES-Hydro, which use_fates_moss forbids.
!
! It is a once-daily sample taken at the dynamics call, not a diurnal mean -- which is
! also the cadence and the moment at which hydraulic-failure mortality reads btran, so it
! is the right sample to read FATES_MORTALITY_HYDRAULIC_PF against.

hist_fincl1 += 'FATES_BTRAN_PF'

! Layer soil temperature, liquid water, ice and matric potential. CLM fields rather than
! FATES ones, like RAIN above, and requested for the same kind of reason: the quantity that
! decides moss's btran is not on the tape unless it is put there.
!
! With the top-layer rooting profile moss's btran is a function of soil layer 1 alone, and
! it reaches exactly zero by three routes. Only the first of them also exempts
! hydraulic-failure mortality, so the other two can kill the cohort:
!
!   - layer 1 at or below tfrz - 2 K, which drops it from root uptake altogether. FATES
!     decides that in get_active_suction_layers, and CLM then computes no suction for the
!     layer at all -- clmfates_interfaceMod fills smp_sl only on the active ones. This is
!     also the mortality's frozen-soil exemption, so a zero btran here is harmless.
!   - the liquid volume CLM hands FATES going to zero, which is NOT the same thing as
!     SOILLIQ going to zero. calc_effective_soilporosity forms
!     eff_porosity = watsat - vol_ice with no floor, and calc_volumetric_h2oliq then caps
!     vol_liq = min(eff_porosity, h2osoi_liq/(dz*denh2o)) -- both in
!     biogeophys/SoilMoistStressMod.F90. So once layer-1 ice reaches watsat*denice*dz,
!     bc_in%h2o_liqvol_sl(1) is exactly zero however much liquid the layer holds.
!   - the suction of the liquid that is there reaching fates_nonhydro_smpsc = -255000 mm,
!     at which btran_ed's max(smpsc, smp) clamp makes the root resistance identically zero.
!
! None of the three was separable from the tape before these lines. FATES_MOSS_FWET_SOIL_TOT
! counts total water, ice included, so a layer whose pore space is solid ice reads as wet.
!
! SOILPSI is not the suction btran sees and should not be compared with smpsc directly. It
! divides layer liquid volume by watsat (biogeophys/HydrologyNoDrainageMod.F90) where the
! root-resistance path divides by eff_porosity, so wherever there is ice SOILPSI is the more
! negative of the two; and it is clipped to [-15, 0] MPa, with -15 assigned outright
! wherever liquid water is zero. Reconstructing the form btran uses needs WATSAT, SUCSAT and
! BSW, which CLM writes to the first history file of a run.
!
! All four are daily means while FATES_BTRAN_PF is a once-daily instantaneous sample, so a
! daily mean can straddle a threshold the sampled value never crossed.
!
! TSOI, SOILLIQ and SOILICE are registered active by default, so those three lines change
! nothing on the FATES-SP tests, which carry the full default CLM field list already; it is
! the I2000Clm60Fates nocomp entries, where clm/Fates sets hist_empty_htapes, that need them
! named. SOILPSI is different: it is registered use_default='inactive', and only under
! use_cn or use_fates (biogeophys/SoilStateType.F90), so its line is what turns it on, on
! every test composing this testmod.

hist_fincl1 += 'TSOI'
hist_fincl1 += 'SOILLIQ'
hist_fincl1 += 'SOILICE'
hist_fincl1 += 'SOILPSI'

! Second history tape (written as h1), 12-hourly with one model year per file, to check
! that the moss wetness proxies change within the day. Until the proxies are sampled
! sub-daily they hold their daily values through each day, so the two records of a day
! are equal.
!
! Only the fields named below land on tape 2: only tape 1 has a default-active field set,
! and fields reach any other tape solely through its hist_fincl, with or without
! hist_empty_htapes. These use `+=` like every other line here.

hist_nhtfrq(2) = -12
hist_mfilt(2)  = 730
hist_fincl2 += 'FATES_GPP_PF'
hist_fincl2 += 'FATES_MOSS_FWET_LIQ'
hist_fincl2 += 'FATES_MOSS_FWET_TOT'
hist_fincl2 += 'FATES_MOSS_FWET_SOIL_LIQ'
hist_fincl2 += 'FATES_MOSS_FWET_SOIL_TOT'
hist_fincl2 += 'FATES_MOSS_FWET_CANOPY'
hist_fincl2 += 'FATES_MOSS_WETNESS_SCALER'
